      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The results of studying the excretion of testosterone and other androgens with the urine after a chorionic gonadotropin load in patients with ischemic heart disease and in persons who had suffered from acute myocardial infarction are discussed. In choriogonin load stimulating the gonads, there is noticeable variability in the excretion of testosterone and epitestosterone, androstenedione, and 7-keto-dehydroepiandrosterone in the urine. The data obtained are evidence of reduced functional reserves of the sex glands in some of the patients."},
